---
include: ["AGENT.global.md"]
---
=== assertion ===
---
name: Global agent file keeps its rules
---
AGENT.global.md is the instruction file loaded into every agent session on
this machine. Compare it against the PR base with git. Check that every
prohibition and requirement (never / always / must / do not, and each bullet
in "The hard rules, at a glance") present in the base is still present in
the head with the same boundary, or that the head moved it to a clearly
equivalent place. A rule that was deleted, softened ("never" to "prefer"),
narrowed, or given a new exception is a violation unless the head states the
same boundary elsewhere. Rewording, reordering and deduplication that keep
the boundary are fine. Name each lost or weakened rule and the section it
left.

=== assertion ===
---
name: Global agent file at-a-glance list matches its sections
---
In AGENT.global.md, "The hard rules, at a glance" is a summary of the
sections below it. Check that every bullet in it is stated by some section,
with the same meaning, and that no section states a hard never/always rule
that the list omits. A bullet that says more or less than its section is a
violation. Name the bullet or section that disagrees.

=== assertion ===
---
name: Global agent file carries no incident anecdotes
severity_cap: warn
---
AGENT.global.md should state rules and the failure each one prevents, not
retell incidents. Flag newly added text in the head (versus the PR base) that
narrates a specific past event: a dated story, a PR or issue number cited as
the occasion, or a blow-by-blow of who did what. One clause naming the
failure a rule prevents is fine. Name the passage.
